      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0038" n="art0038">
        <head>BOWLING.</head>
        <p>BOWLING.</p>
        <p>ffIARRINGTON AND DISTRICV ASSOCIATION.</p>
        <p>INDIVIDUAL MERIT COMPETITION.</p>
        <p>The first round of this competition was opened on Rylands' green on Saturday, in ideal weather, in the presence of 200 or 300 spectators. Befoie the game opened, the referee Mr. George Ball, jun.. said that that was the first competition of its kind ever held in Warrington and he hoped that the players would endeavour to make it a great success. Ho also hoped that they would conduct the competition in a sports- manlike manner. The most interesting game of the afternoon was between B. Jolley, of Runcorn, and G. Hatton, of Whitecross Recreation, which after an exciting finish, resulted in a victory for Jolley by two points. The following are the results:— - R. 4ntrobus 2l W. Ball 16 J. Berry 2l S. Leigh J. Sudlow 2l W. H. Eyes R. Sunderland G. Holbrook 2l A. Vernon . R. Rothwell. H. Eyes 2l H. Smith l7 _ . - --</p>
