      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0040" n="art0040">
        <head>WARRINGTON MAN IN THE FINAL.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON MAN IN THE FINAL.</p>
        <p>At the Sandon Hotel, Liverpool, on Tuesday evening the final rounds of the Liverpool Association merit competition were decided. The finalists were Alec Raisbeck (Sandon, the well-known international foot- baller), and A. Gleave. a popular Warrington and Newton-le-Willows bowler. The green was in splendid order and the bowling of a particularly high standard. Raisheck had the lock of the jack in the opening end of the final, but his opponent scored with a dead length. Play was in favour of the footballer until 18-5 had been called. Gleave, however, with a double and three singles, made his score double figures. He made a plucky light, hut at the 25th end Raisbeelc ran out a popular winner as follows : —Raisbeck, 21; Gleave, 11.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>SHEPEII4:RDS' MAIN,</head>
        <p>SHEPEII4:RDS' MAIN,</p>
        <p>Saturday wit ressed the third annual bowling main for the G reenal I Challenge Cup and gold modal presented by Councillor Fulton-Smith, for competition among the members of the Warrington District of the Loyal Order of Ancient Shepherds. The games were played at the Stag Inn, Walton, under most favourable conditions. There weie 79 entrants, who spent a most enjoyable time. The district officers present were Bro. James Gillooley, D.P.C.S. Bro. William Miles, and Dis. -nem, Bro. James Parr. The Prov. Cor. Sec. Bro. P. Edg•ir was absent owing to indisposition. Tne Bowling Main Committee consisted of the following :—P.C.S. jamea Gillooley, chairman; D.P.C.S. Bro. W. Miles, deputy-chairman ; Bro. P. Edgar, secretary ; Bro. P. L. Edgar, assistant secretary; Bro. Parr, treasurer ; Bros. 'l'. C. Duckworth, R. H. Holford, P. Harbourne, T. Baskerville, jun.' James Atkinson, W. Lswler, Joseph Ad uus, Joseph Ashton, John Parr, William Massey, J. Mather, H. Bate, D. Harris, T. Miller, W. Hall, F. Yates and A. Pusill. The catering of Bro. J. C. Shaw gave great satisfaction. The competition throughout was most interesting,and some of the gimes were exceptioll4ll7 keen. Last year's winner, E. North, Was beaten in the senti,linal by Harry Twiss by 13-5. The other tie in the semi-final was between Herbert Twiss and W. Stringer and the latter went down by 13-8. Two brothers—Harry and Herbert Twiss—figured in the final. After give-and-take play Harry led by 10-9. A double to Herbert placed him ahead, and the subse- quent two games resulted in a point each, so that Herbert Twiss is the champion for 1909. • The following were the various rounds : FIRST ROUND.</p>
        <p>WI. Leigh (Far.) T. Miller (I) J. Adams (scr) l3 P..Harbourne(l) •• 6 John Higham (3) G. Higham (scr) l3 John Edwardson (3) .. 5 J. Gilooley (5) P. Gilooley (3) T. Ilaskerville jun. (4)... 13 J. Shakeshaft (4) H. Lawton (2) • 13 James Warburton (2)... 8 W. Adcroft (2) l3 E Stockton (6) J. Kenwright (2) l3 W. 11. Moorcroft (5) ... 9 J. E. Shaw (scr) l3. T. Baskerville, sen. (3) 9 James.Howarth (scr) Harry 'rwiss (owed 1) ... 13 James Lawton (I) W. Lawler (1) l3 R. H. Holford (1) P. Lowe (4) l3 A. Push! (4) lO T. Gallop (3) . There was a large number of byes. SECOND ROUND.</p>
        <p>P. L. Edgar (3) J. H. Brown (3) l3 G. Warburton jun. (2)... 7 H. Massey (3) l3 A. Duckworth (3) Thomas Webb (3) F. Yates (4) D. Harris (5) W. Lawler (1) l3 E. Cotterall (3) - 4 J. Winstanley (1) R. Fairbrotber sen. (scr) 13 Joseph Higham (3) 9 W. Howard (1) D. W. Lee (1) W. Jones (4) J. T. HarrisOn (scr) J. Kenwright (2) Herbert Twiss (scr) R. Warburton (2) " 13 T. Baskerville, jun. (4) 5 Joseph Ashton (2) l3 Ben Higbam (2) ll J. C. Shaw (set.) J. W. Hayward (4) l3 P. Gillooley (3) 6 Joseph Howard (scr) l3 Joseph Matthew (5) ... 9 W. Stringer (4) W. Adcroft (2) l3 W. Hitch (2) ll T. Miller (4) W. Leigh (scr) l3 II Fairbrother (1) John Lingard (2) Harry Twiss (owed 1)... 13 James Atkinson(l) 9 Fred Lowe (4) J. Adams (scr) E. North (1) • 8</p>
        <p>. , THIRD ROUND. W. Jones W. Lawler J. H. Brown l3 D. W. Lee R. Warburton l3 W. Adcroft T. Miller l3 John Hussey 8 Herbert Twiss P. L. Edgar l3 Joseph Howarth 9 E. North l3 J. Winstanley lO T. Webb l3 D. Harris R. Fairbrother (sen.) .. 13 J. Adams Harry Twiss J. W. Hayward John Linmird l3 W. Leigh J. T. Harrison W. Stringer J. Kenwright - 13 H. Howard</p>
        <p>_ FOURTH ROUND. R. Fairbrother, sen. W. Lawler J. W. Hayward J. T. Harrison Herbert Twiss l3 J. Kenwrigbt • 3 E. North l3 John Lingard W. Stringer . l3 P. L. Edgar 9 _ _ ....</p>
