      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0086" n="art0086">
        <head>Do You Get up with a Bad Back? Are you Dropsical? Rheumatic? Always Tired? Read this Warrington Woman's Experience.</head>
        <p>Do You Get up with a Bad Back? Are you Dropsical? Rheumatic? Always Tired? Read this Warrington Woman's Experience.</p>
        <p>No one know i the suffering some women quietly endure. They think it is only natural for them to have pain in the back, throbbing headaches, dizzy spells, rheumatic twinges, irregular heart, and to feel tired and worn out before the day is half through. And so they bear up as best they can, in patience and without complaint, never thinking they can be cured—never suspecting the kidneys as the cause of their illness.</p>
        <p>But it is not right for women to be always ailing, and the best proof of this is given in the outspoken statements of local women who have been made well, and kept well, by Doan's Backache Kidney Pills, the great kidney and bladder medicine for men .and women, old and young. Doan's pills gently heal the tired, over-worked kidneys, and when the kidneys are well they take out the urinous poisons which cause the above symptoms as well as bladder and urinary disorders, gravel, dropsy, rheumatism, lumbago, and wasting away. Over seren years bad gene by since her cure by Dean's pills, when Mrs. M. Welch, 27, Dolman's-lane. Warrington, said :—" have always recommended Dean's pills; they do me a great deal of good. Now and again I get cold in the kidneys, but a box of the pills always cures me."</p>
        <p>The statement made by Mrs. Welch at the time of her cure, ran :—" You are quite welcome to publish toy testimonial for Doan's pills, and I hope it will be the moans of others trying the medicine. My ailment was kidney disorder, and the symptoms were bad pains in my back and loins, dim- ness of sight, giddiness, and urinary trouble. I was very low and feebli, and 1 has] to take hold of the furniture when I moved about the house. Specks seemed to be floating before my eyes, and I felt full of wind. _ _ _</p>
        <p>_ " I consulted a doctor, and he told me my kidneys were diseased, and I should have to be careful or dropsy would set in. He give me some medicine, but I got no better, and as time went on I grew worse. "When I began with Doan's pills I did not get much benefit from the first box, but I persevered with the medicine, and with the second box I began to improve. Gradually the pains left me, my simht became clearer,and the kidney secretions were natural. I have derived more benefit from Doan's pills than from all the medicine I tried. I shall do what I can to recommend the pills. Of all chemists and stores, or direct from the proprietors Foster-McClellan Co., 8, Wells-street, Oxford-street, London, W., at 2a. 9d. per box, or las. Dd. for six boxes.</p>
        <p>ASK FOR DOAN'S AND GET DOAN'S LIKE Mrs. WELCH HAD.</p>
      </div>
