      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0116" n="art0116">
        <head>COLOURS FOR THE TERRITORIALS.</head>
        <p>COLOURS FOR THE TERRITORIALS.</p>
        <p>The stately walls of Windsor Castle looked down on an impressive spectacle on Saturday afternoon, when His Majesty presented colours to the 108 units of the Territorial Army which had qualified to receive their, flags at the hands of the King. Field Marshals, Generals, and Cabinet Ministers in Windsor uniform were in attendance, and foreign officers were present from such widely-separated States as Japan and the Argentine Republic. At the conclusion of the ceremony regulars and territorials bared their heads ad We three riugiog cheers fur His Majesty.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0117" n="art0117">
        <p>KING'S PORTRAIT FOR THE QUEEN.</p>
        <p>PROFESSOR TUXEN, DANISH PAINTER.</p>
        <p>His Majesty the King has promised some sittings to the Danish painter, Professor Tuxen. The new portrait of his Majesty is to be especially painted for the Tucen, and Professor Tuxen was the artist chosen by hcr Majesty. Professor Tuxen has now arrived in London to carry out his commission.</p>
