      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0119" n="art0119">
        <head>PRETTY GOWNS AT ASCOT.</head>
        <p>PRETTY GOWNS AT ASCOT.</p>
        <p>The fashionable world was seen at its best at Ascot. The dresses seemed to be even more beautiful than ever before, and the hats were of course wonderful to look upon—some of them were like cartwheels, others resembled upturned waste-paper baskets, and others again were simply flower gardens of rare and tropical blooms.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0120" n="art0120">
        <head>SKIN DISEASES</head>
        <p>SKIN DISEASES</p>
        <p>OVERCOME BY THE WONDERFUL BLOOD PURIFYING. PROPERTIES OF DR. MORSE'S INDIAN ROOT PILLS.</p>
        <p>A person suffering from eruptions of the skin has much to endure. It is not merely the dis- comfiture and irritation and painful but life is made misera- ble by depression of spirits. The liver is torpid and the kidneys are partially inoperative, and you feel languid and weak. The disease is in the blood and when the system is not cleansed through the usual channels Nature asserts herself and forces portions of the impurities through the skin in the form of Pimples, Boils, and Blotches. External remedies—powders, oint- ments and lotions only alleviate; they do not get at the cause. Dr. Morse's Indian Root Pills get at the cause by removing the disease from the blood. They cleanse the system by stimulating the Liver and strengthening the Kidneys, which filter the blood and throw off the impure matter through the regular channels. They are a positive and permanent cure for all complaints arising from impure blood, liver and kidney complaints. - Sold by Chemists and Stores, price 1/11 per bottle, or The W. H. Comstock Co., iftd., 21, Parringdon Avenue, Ifonkn, EC.</p>
