        <p>ST. THOMAS' CHURCH SUNDAY SCHOOL TEACHERS' PICNIC.--A picnic promoted by the teachers at this Sunday school was held on Saturday, Llangollen being the resort visited. The party, numbering 41, travelled in a G.W.R. saloon attached to the 8.17 a.m. train from Bank Quay Station and arrived at Llangollen soon after 10 a.m. Though rain was falling when they left home, the weather was all that could be desired by the • time they reached Llangollen. After arriving at :Llangollen they dispersed in different directions" meeting at 12.30 for dinner at the Royal Hotel. In the afternoon they all went for a very pleasant drive, spending some time at Berwyn, and came back in time for tea at the hotel at -five o'clock. Warrington was reached at 9.20 after a highly successful outing.</p>
        <p>_ . GARDEN §OCIETY.—The members of the Stockton Heath Garden Society had permission to visit Appleton Hall grounds ' and gardens on Thursday evening. Unfortunately, unfavourable -weather prevailed, but notwithstanding this fact some fifty members paid the visit and were SO well rewarded for venturing forth. The grounds and gardens were found to be in splendid condition, looking all the more attractive for the refreshing rain. Mr. and Mrs. Lyon were in residence and the party. were pleased to learn that Mr. Lyon keeps in excellent health. but regretted to be informed that Mrs. Lyon was indisposed, suffering from the effects of a chill. PRESENTATION TO COUNCILLOR W. B. ROBERTS.— Councillor W. B. Roberta will next week retire from the position of head brewer at Wilderspool after 24 years' service, lie is, we understand, going to live at Lymm. He will be succeeded at the Brewery by Mr. C. S. Stone, the under-brewer. The staff were enter- tained by Mr. Roberts to dinner at the Saracen's Head on Thursday evening, and took advantage of the opportunity of showing their great esteem for him by presenting him with a massive silver salver. Mr. F. Peaison spoke feelingly of the great regard in which Mr. Roberts was held by the staff, and the presentation was made in suitable terms by Mr. F. Howard. Mr, Roberts, who was much touched by the many kind things said about him, replied. To-night the Brewery workmen will present Mr. Roberts with an address and a sther rose bowl.</p>
