        <p>Rixton. A, .HoUst INN.—At the meeting of the Licensing for the West Derby Hundred 'at Liverpool fow;:tes,(lBY, the 11Innenester Shin Canal Company _iree„,—') supported the application for renewal of the ItixTe of the Boathouse Inn, Ship Canal Erni ankment, btu. the bench referred it for compensation.— klreaves Lord represented the justices. • Walton. (I•FiTur°ißnoYS' Tim..—Tbe choir boys of St. John's. Ida ch, Walton, had their annual trip on Monday, theadildno being visited. The party, accompanied by L. J. T. and Mrs. Darwall, left Bank QTI.Y on shortly alter 7.30 and reached their destination potrod After an excellent dinner had beendieta,ke!) of, the afternoon was spent as inclination ret, and all thoroughly enjoyed themselves. The - 14,412,11 journey was commenced at an earlier hour than , and the boys reached home at about 8.30.</p>
        <p>Croft. UNITARIAN CHAPEL AND SellooL.—The Ifld sermons "ere preached in the above place on Lived' I'st• The preacher, Rev. T. Lloyd Jones, of gave two very helpful addresses. The music tatt:ndered.by Warrington choir who gave the th,,, entitled " God is a spirit, and they that worship t4eneetln„ust worship Him in spirit and. in. tr,i2tl! 4so, v and• in the evening "Teach me, ti clod. vidocl :riends came up from ' Warrington by bus pro- •t10 '°r the occasion. The collections amounted to 8. 4d.</p>
        <p>'Appleton. • n Saturday evening a fire brrle out Appleton, the residence of Mr. Alan lt 41X1 78„xed ;,61.- The Wilderspool Brigade Ali's. sunirrored Out with commendable promptitude, i tinderthe hrtn lreetion of Engineer Briggs. On arrival at the itontaitil,e3T found the neighbours at work with bucketsZheat-tilila+4k water and tne fire, which was confined to •,ith -ee stairs of the house, had been got under t(LiLltuch damage having been dore. It appears RS."7, family left home at about 7.30, and shortly 4111 ,"rius neighbours saw smoke issuing from a window, 111"3r lt;Ze into the house. The save is regarded as a Y one.</p>
        <p>ztw. Culcheth. r thool PTURCH PARISH CHURCH.—The annual Sunday L. i kerMons were preached in this church on R""rviee„" Preacher for the morning and afternoon '41311-- WaS the Rev. C. NV. Mercer, M.A., of St. T, - "8 II 1 the Rev. Leonard p o me, and • the evening :I v 4 arr A Isl•A_,of St.Jobn's, Altrincham. The anthems when they said unto mo " (Etrey) and ;,4411 der:alse the Lord " (Marks) were very effectively ;"'eo 11 the choir. The Magnificat (Simper) was er,,-",;1 with much feeling, the solo being ably `irnie 'Miss Annie Maddock of Newchurch. Mr. J. itgatittociated at the organ. There were large con- -"uht.-18 at all the services and the collections which to £37 10s. were in aid of the Sunday schopl.</p>
