        <p>LONDON, THIIRSDAY.—At the Central Dead Meat Market to-day the beef trade was firm. Scotch long sides sold at 4s 4d to 4s 6d., and short sides 9s 8d to ss; English sides 3s lid to 4s 2d ; United States sides— Liverpool killed 3s 10d to 4s id, and Deptford killed 3s lid to 4s Id; American hindquarters 4s 4d to 4s 7d. and forequarters 2s 7d to 2s 9d. Mutton a quiet sale ; Scotch tegs 4s 8d to ss, wethers 4s 8d to 5s ; English small wethers 4s 2d to 486 d, and even 2s ad to 2s 10d.</p>
