      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0172" n="art0172">
        <head>CATTLE.</head>
        <p>CATTLE.</p>
        <p>LONDON (METROPOLITAN), THURSDAM—Beef trade quiet. Sheep quiet, 7,-; to 8 stone down wefhers, clipped, 5s to 5s 2d; exceptionally, 53 4d; 9 stone ditto, ss; 10 stone down ewes, 3s 4d to 3s 6d; 11 stone half- bred ditto, 3s 2d to 3s 4d. Calves quiet, but making 53 2d per 8113.</p>
        <p>DUBLIN, THURSDAY.—On sale: Beasts, 1,892; sheep, 8,495; veal calves, 37. Cattle met a goad trade at late rates ; beef, 46s to 47s per cwt. Sheep quiet and unchanged, with a fair inquiry; nice hoggets mutton, 41d to 63d per lb. Lambs firmer at 22s to 36s each. Pigs net so strong. Veal slow and cheaper. CHEESE.</p>
        <p>NANTWICH, THURSDAY.—There was a pitch of about 80 tons. and buyers were well represented. Best dairies made from 56s to Gls per cwt. Medium from 50s to 555; and lower grades down to 47s 6d.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-06-26_WidnesExaminer_art0173" n="art0173">
